  "lineage": "Interactive score composed for game hardware, from the 1980 arcade and 1983-1994 console chip era — Koichi Sugiyama, Nobuo Uematsu, Koji Kondo and Yuzo Koshiro writing three-to-eight-voice PSG and FM parts under strict polyphony and memory limits — through the CD and streamed-audio era after 1995; the persistent markers are short seamlessly loopable cues, fast arpeggiated pseudo-chords standing in for missing voices, wide leaps and rapid modal modulation to stay memorable at 120-160 BPM, and layered or branching arrangements that respond to player state.",
